WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.249
Some questions deserve more than a quick answer. HiExplore is built around

2
00:00:04.249 --> 00:00:07.082
one idea: give your curiosity a longer life.

3
00:00:07.791 --> 00:00:12.371
A question can wait quietly, keeping its context and open questions. The

4
00:00:12.371 --> 00:00:16.568
goal is long-term background research, once a cloud worker is connected.

5
00:00:17.291 --> 00:00:21.749
New experiment data. A relevant paper. Evidence that challenges a belief. Or

6
00:00:21.749 --> 00:00:26.208
new input from you. These are reasons to reconsider, not reasons to

7
00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:27.322
invent a breakthrough.

8
00:00:28.041 --> 00:00:32.999
The project manager decides whether to investigate. Agents analyze the material, check

9
00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:37.956
the evidence, and audit the conclusions. If evidence is missing, they wait.

10
00:00:38.666 --> 00:00:43.076
In our real cooling-room example, the audit challenged an overstated citation. No

11
00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:47.487
room experiment had been run. The useful outcome was clearer limits, and

12
00:00:47.487 --> 00:00:49.324
a request for real data.

13
00:00:50.041 --> 00:00:55.629
Verified evidence can support a revised judgment, after review. Quiet between meaningful

14
00:00:55.629 --> 00:00:58.424
changes. Ready when it matters. HiExplore.